<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Suessetani</h1><p class="st-meta">500 BCE – 184 BCE (approx.) · capital Corbio</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A little-known people of the Cinco Villas region of Aragon, whose town Corbio fell to Rome in 184 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Suessetani lived north of the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a>, probably in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cinco-villas">Cinco Villas</a> area of modern Aragon, between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sedetani">Sedetani</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vascones">Vascones</a>. Their origins and language are uncertain; some scholars think they were of Celtic rather than Iberian stock. They appear only in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy's</a> account of the Roman wars.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of their institutions beyond their main town, Corbio. They joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ilergetes">Ilergetes</a> in raids and in the anti-Roman revolts of the early 2nd century BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 184 BCE the Roman praetor Aulus Terentius Varro captured Corbio and sold its inhabitants into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>. The Suessetani disappear from history soon afterwards, and their lands seem to have passed to neighbouring peoples, possibly the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vascones">Vascones</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 500 BCE – 184 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:49.75%;width:6.29%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt>